  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Runtime vs static dependencies",
      "items": [
        "Arrows are runtime calls observed at call sites (HTTP, SQL, SMTP, driver connections).",
        "Static only: the web UI's typed client (frontend/src/api/schema.d.ts) is generated at build time from the backend OpenAPI spec (python -m dawam openapi); no runtime web → app call.",
        "Static only: modules import each other only through their package; composition roots (app.py, worker.py, wiring.py, job_handlers.py) wire cross-module hooks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Auth & trust boundaries",
      "items": [
        "Only edge publishes a port; app trusts X-Forwarded-* from edge's fixed IP alone (compose.yaml, app.py ProxyHeadersMiddleware).",
        "Every /api/v1 route requires the CSRF token; routes taking CurrentUser need the dawam_session cookie. Per-Workspace roles are enforced in the workspaces policy (can / authorize).",
        "Credentials (source passwords, LLM keys) are sealed with AES-256-GCM (platform/crypto.py SecretBox)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Agentic layer",
      "items": [
        "Loop: each model turn may call tools; results go back to the model until it answers or hits the tool-call cap. Long chats are fitted to the window and older turns summarised (compaction).",
        "Routing: short plain questions go to the light model, others to the agent model (routing.py). Models without native tool calling get prompted tool calls (prompted.py).",
        "Tools: 39 (catalog, profiles, lineage, run_source_query, files, KPIs, Change Set proposals, remember/recall memory, web_search/web_fetch, plans, ask_member, start_job). Each call is checked against the Workspace data-sharing level and the user's permission; results are checked for prompt injection.",
        "RAG: documents are cut into passages, indexed with Postgres full-text and pgvector embeddings (worker index jobs); search fuses both rankings. The first chat message gets top passages automatically when enabled.",
        "Jobs: start_job runs a task in the worker; behind a flag a supervisor plans and delegates to specialists (supervisor.py)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "LLM providers: self-hosted vs external",
      "items": [
        "Each provider is marked internal (self-hosted) or external by the admin (llm_providers.is_internal).",
        "Self-hosted examples: Ollama, vLLM, SGLang, LM Studio, llama.cpp server, all through the openai_compatible adapter.",
        "External examples: OpenAI, OpenRouter, Groq, Mistral (openai_compatible), Anthropic Claude, Azure OpenAI, Google Gemini / Vertex AI, AWS Bedrock.",
        "An internal-only Workspace refuses external models for every role, so its data never leaves the network."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Inferred or unknown",
      "items": [
        "Resolved: the API calls source DBs directly only for the connection test; model-written SQL comes from the assistant tool run_source_query via SourceQueryService, in the app for chat and in the worker for assistant tasks (see the source-db-flows diagram).",
        "Worker → SMTP: not observed (no mail service wired in worker or job handlers).",
        "Ollama, Mailpit, the demo source DB and the GPU override depend on the Compose file and profile used (compose.yaml, deploy/docker-compose.yaml, deploy/docker-compose.gpu.yaml).",
        "Storage backend (volume vs S3) and which LLM providers exist are deployment configuration, not fixed in code."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
